  "id": "COMPOUND:20347 - PROTEIN:6311",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ailantinol G may interact with Histone deacetylase 5 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are expressed in LoVo cells. These intermediates, including N-[(3S,4R,5R,8S,9S,10R,13S,14S,17S)-17-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-3,4-dimethylpent-3-enamide and 1-[3-(Dimethoxymethoxy)-4-hydroxyphenyl]-7-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)hepta-1,6-diene-3,5-dione, are all known to target Histone deacetylase 5. The consistent score of 0.6606 across the three paths indicates a strong, albeit indirect, relationship between Ailantinol G and Histone deacetylase 5, likely mediated through the LoVo cell line. The mechanisms involve the inhibition of Histone deacetylase 5 by these intermediates, which may suggest a broader role for Ailantinol G in modulating histone acetylation and potentially influencing gene expression. The evidence supports a plausible pathway where Ailantinol G acts as a modulator of Histone deacetylase 5 through its interaction with these intermediate compounds, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
